{"surah": 105, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَٰبِ ٱلْفِيلِ ", "translation": "Have you not considered, [O Muḥammad], how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَرَ", "translit": "َrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِأَصْحَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰḥْṣَaʾِb", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْفِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِfْlٱ", "root": "فيل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "أَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِى تَضْلِيلٍ ", "translation": "Did He not make their plan into misguidance?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَجْعَلْ", "translit": "ْlَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَيْدَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَضْلِيلٍ", "translit": "ٍlyِlْḍَt", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ ", "translation": "And He sent against them birds in flocks,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَرْسَلَ", "translit": "َlَsْrَaʾَw", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "طَيْرًا", "translit": "āًrْyَṭ", "root": "طير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَبَابِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِbāَbَaʾ", "root": "ابل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "تَرْمِيهِم بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّن سِجِّيلٍ ", "translation": "Striking them with stones of hard clay,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَرْمِيهِم", "translit": "mِhyِmْrَt", "root": "رمي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِحِجَارَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَrāَjgِḥِb", "root": "حجر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سِجِّيلٍ", "translit": "ٍlyِّjgِs", "root": "سجل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "فَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَّأْكُولٍۭ ", "translation": "And He made them like eaten straw.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَجَعَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَʿعَjgَf", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَعَصْفٍ", "translit": "ٍfْṣَʿعَk", "root": "عصف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّأْكُولٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭlwُkْaʾَّm", "root": "اكل"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "وهذه القصص وردت في القرآن لتعرف بها سنة الله في عباده الذي خلوا من قبل، فما في القرآن شيء إلا وهو هدى ونور وتعرف من الله تعالى إلى خلقه، فتارة يتعرف إليهم بالتقديس فيقول: \" قل هو الله أحد الله الصمد لم يلد ولم يولد ولم يكن له كفواً أحد \" وتارة يتعرف إليهم بصفات جلاله فيقول: \" الملك القدوس السلام المؤمن المهيمن العزيز الجبار المتكبر \" وتارة يتعرف إليهم في أفعاله المخوفة والمرجوة فيتلو عليهم سنته في أعدائه وفي أنبيائه فيقول: \" ألم تر كيف فعل ربك بعاد إرم ذات العماد - ألم تر كيف فعل ربك بأصحاب الفي", "english": "And these stories have come in the Quran so that you may know through them the Way (Sunnah) of Allah in His servants who have passed before. There is nothing in the Quran except that it is guidance and light and a recognition from Allah the Exalted to His creation. At times He makes Himself known to them through Sanctification (Taqdis) when He says: \"Say: He is Allah, the One, Allah, the Eternal Refuge. He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent.\" And at times He makes Himself known to them through His attributes of Majesty (Jalal) when He says: \"The Sovereign, the Holy, the Peace, the Faithful, the Overseer, the Exalted in Might, the Compeller, the Superior.\" And at times He makes Himself known to them in His actions that are feared and hoped for, and He recites to them His Way (Sunnah) regarding His enemies and His prophets when He says: \"Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with 'Aad of Iram - of the great pillars? Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant?\"", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Dhikr"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 1047], [2, 1047, 1483], [3, 1483, 2245], [4, 2245, 2942], [5, 2942, 3759], [6, 3759, 5122], [7, 5122, 6167]], "2": [[1, 350, 968], [2, 968, 1925], [3, 1925, 2969], [4, 2969, 3452], [5, 3452, 4573]], "3": [[1, 350, 1385], [2, 1385, 2384], [3, 2384, 3348], [4, 3348, 4651]], "4": [[1, 350, 2335], [2, 2335, 4351], [3, 4351, 5421], [4, 5421, 7081]], "5": [[1, 350, 1783], [2, 1783, 2840], [3, 2840, 4521]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 400, 1536], [2, 1536, 2246], [3, 2246, 3488], [4, 3488, 4624], [5, 4624, 5955], [6, 5955, 8177], [7, 8177, 9882]], "2": [[1, 400, 1513], [2, 1513, 3235], [3, 3235, 5114], [4, 5114, 5984], [5, 5984, 8002]], "3": [[1, 400, 2443], [2, 2443, 4416], [3, 4416, 6318], [4, 6318, 8890]], "4": [[1, 400, 3050], [2, 3050, 5742], [3, 5742, 7171], [4, 7171, 9386]], "5": [[1, 400, 3030], [2, 3030, 4970], [3, 4970, 8054]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 400, 1148], [2, 1148, 1615], [3, 1615, 2456], [4, 2456, 3216], [5, 3216, 4093], [6, 4093, 5596], [7, 5596, 6940]], "2": [[1, 450, 1154], [2, 1154, 2463], [3, 2463, 3673], [4, 3673, 4245], [5, 4245, 5710]], "3": [[1, 280, 1566], [2, 1566, 2669], [3, 2669, 3926], [4, 3926, 5710]], "4": [[1, 180, 2243], [2, 2243, 4390], [3, 4390, 5294], [4, 5294, 7060]], "5": [[1, 220, 1903], [2, 1903, 3135], [3, 3135, 5270]]}}, "letterTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"105:1": [{"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 0, "char": "أ", "grapheme": "أَ", "start": 350, "end": 611, "duration": 261, "peakTime": 480}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 1, "char": "ل", "grapheme": "لَ", "start": 611, "end": 829, "duration": 218, "peakTime": 720}, {"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 2, 